     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** at a different frequency\n- Something else\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose on purpose. I'd still advise against it."
      }
     ],
